## Span decomposition

### CAPACITY

The span adds **74.611257 Gbit** and reduces energy by **1844.322712 J**. Using the exact path decomposition that first credits the numerator change at baseline energy and then credits the energy change at the final numerator:

| component | EE contribution (Mbit/J) | relative to baseline EE | share of total EE gain |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| extra credited bits | 1.089739 | +13.41% | 81.03% |
| reduced energy | 0.255089 | +3.14% | 18.97% |
| total | 1.344829 | +16.55% | 100.00% |

Per-user delivery is **not nondecreasing** over all 800 user-anchor comparisons for this selector: 39 decreases; minimum delta -769.880451 Mbit. Therefore the reduced-energy component is positive for the reported numerator, but the stronger any-numerator guarantee does not follow.

### DEMAND_CAPPED

