.scratch/joint-c3-v011/FABLE-51-SHORT-C3-ADJUDICATION-PROMPT.md:5:The final objective is ratio-of-sums EE, total delivered bits divided by total network energy. Deployment is immutable: exactly three independent 28-action heads, one common safe mask, unweighted Q1+Q2+Q3, one argmax and one action. No mixer, weights, coordinator, sign flip or post-training override. C1 owns focal current bits plus all current network-energy difference. OPS3-C2 provisionally owns focal projected future bits, marginal future network energy and persistence risk. Therefore C3 must not numerically count either energy term again. A future Q3 may use decision-time physical state only.
.scratch/joint-c3-v011/FABLE-51-SHORT-C3-ADJUDICATION-PROMPT.md:20:2. Energy-compatible spatial externality: use the same bits-only X but permit a nonzero C3 preference only for a candidate whose insertion has zero marginal canonical network energy (already-active beam/satellite and required RF no greater than the focal-removed beam maximum) over the declared physical offsets; all other candidates receive zero C3 preference. Energy is only a Boolean eligibility condition, never added numerically, to avoid double-counting C1/C2.
.scratch/joint-c3-v011/FABLE-51-SHORT-C3-ADJUDICATION-PROMPT.md:23:You may correct the formulas above. Propose at most two candidates, not two components to combine. For each provide an exact formula with reference/zero/units, ownership proof, why it can avoid the observed energy expansion, allowed learner features, decisive falsifier, and estimated no-training oracle cost. Decide whether C1+OPS3-C2 should remain fixed for this next gate. Specify an ordered non-cherry-picking comparison on new TRAIN worlds whose primary condition is EE(C1+C2+C3)>EE(C1+C2), with service and interaction guards. Do not tune sign, scale, horizon, seed, threshold or order to observed outcomes. Separate facts, inference and proposal.
